## Branches and PRs

- Branch name: `claude/<linear-id-lowercase>-<short-slug>`, e.g. `claude/abc-12-search-page`. The Linear ID in the name lets Linear link the branch.
- One issue, one PR. Keep PRs small. Open as a draft, mark ready when checks pass.
- The PR body starts with `Fixes ABC-12` (the Linear ID), `GitHub issue: #N` and the issue's `Mockup: <link>` line, so Linear links and closes the issue and reviewers can find the design.
- Never push to `main`. PRs merge through GitHub auto-merge once the required checks pass: `check` and `Merge gate` (no `needs-human`, no unresolved review thread, and the latest Claude review says "Verdict: ready to merge"). Never merge around them.
- Never resolve a security thread unless a second, separate Claude check agrees it is fixed or a false alarm.

